# torus_rough.cam — scallop-mode stock_to_leave roughing on the torus
# (DECISIONS.md "stock_to_leave convex mirrors…"). torus.cam's ring run as a
# ROUGHING pass, and the first convex-mirror carrier: the ring-to-ring cusps
# live on the tube meridian, which the ball rides convexly on BOTH halves
# (the concave slice's reclassification), and the tube meridian is a circle —
# so the whole budget is the sphere recipe with the tube radius standing in
# for the sphere's, and the inflated torus is still a torus (R1
# self-offsetting, tube 4 + 0.3).
#
# The 0.5mm allowance is a ceiling on TOTAL remaining material including this
# pass's own cusps (max, not min): scallop=0.2 spends 0.2mm as cusp budget and
# the remaining 0.3mm is nominal skin, so every CL ring sits 7.3mm
# (= 4 + 3 + 0.3) off the tube's centre circle — crown ring at z = 7.300,
# radius 25 (X75.000 / X25.000), the hand-checked anchors. The inner bowl's
# circumferential concavity is the gouge guard's business, checked at the
# roughing offset: 3 + 0.3 = 3.3mm against the 21mm inner-equator radius.
#
# CONTAINED 2026-08-13 (DECISIONS.md "the torus's annulus island…", slice 2):
# stock 2mm proud of the crown and grown in y so the moat lands on it, with T1
# opening the moat and the hole first. This one's Clear leaves 1.0 — the
# finish's own 0.5 allowance plus 0.5 — so the pass behind it is handed real
# skin rather than eating into what it promises to leave. The ring numbers
# above are unchanged: the feature did not move.
units mm
feed 600
plunge 200
rapid_z 9
clearance_z 30
spindle 4000

stock Box(w=100, l=100, h=31, x=0, y=-10, z=6)

tool T1 Endmill(dia=12.0)
tool T9 Ballmill(dia=6.0)

# Torus centre at z=0; major_dia=50, minor_dia=8.
feature T Torus(major_dia=50, minor_dia=8, x=50, y=40, z=0)

run Clear(tool=T1, profile=T, stepover=8.0, stepdown=2.0, stock_to_leave=1.0)
run Copy(tool=T9, surface=T, scallop=0.2, stock_to_leave=0.5)
